[I] Declaratively deploy your Kubernetes manifests

[T] Helmfile is a declarative spec for deploying helm charts. It lets you:
[T] 
[T] - Keep a directory of chart value files and maintain changes in version control.
[T] - Apply CI/CD to configuration changes.
[T] - Periodically sync to avoid skew in environments.
[T] 
[T] To avoid upgrades for each iteration of helm, the helmfile executable
[T] delegates to helm - as a result, helm must be installed.

[U] https://github.com/helmfile/helmfile

[A] mumoshu
[A] itscaro
[A] yxxhero
[A] xiaomudk
[A] zhaque44
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS
[R] + arm arm64 loongarch64 mips mips64 powerpc64 riscv64 s390x x86 x86-64

[L] MIT
[V] 1.8.2

[D] c1ba0c30c53fadb1d738183bc460b3c921b10668212c77fad05b4f45 helmfile-1.8.2.tar.gz https://github.com/helmfile/helmfile/archive/v1.8.2/

. $base/package/*/*/go-conf.in

var_append goconfopt ' ' '-o bin/helmfile -ldflags="-X go.szostok.io/version.version=$ver"'
hook_add postmake 5 "install -v bin/helmfile $root$bindir/"
